{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:694e122ca5e9b4d0","name":"Felucian Shaman Talent Tree","source":{"id":"source:reference-694e122ca5e9b4d0","title":"Felucian Shaman Talent Tree","revision":25738,"timestamp":"2024-12-14T00:35:49Z","sha256":"dc421ab16313440003365139db5eec5d2642b38050913bb6af0c372fa2632bf5","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25738","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Felucian%20Shaman%20Talent%20Tree&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-694e122ca5e9b4d0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Unleashed Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Unleashed_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Felucian Shamans learn to manipulate their natural aptitude with ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," and amplify their inherent powers in a variety of ways. Only Force-users that are part of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Felucian Shamans"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Felucian_Shamans","referenceId":"reference:3f5a6e0e902bd292"}," may select ",{"tag":"a","children":["Talents"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talents","referenceId":"reference:e8871b70ebfa07d9"}," from this tree.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Core Talents"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Felucian Charm Beast"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You may use a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check in place of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persuasion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persuasion","referenceId":"reference:196fbdc5f1823320"}," check when attempting to change the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," of an undomesticated creature with an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Intelligence"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Intelligence"}," of 2 or less. Additionally, you do not take the normal -5 penalty on the check if the creature can't speak or understand your language.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Felucian Command Beast"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"b","children":["Felucian Charm Beast"]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Whenever you manage to shift the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attitude"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attitude"}," of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," to Indifferent or Friendly, you may treat that creature as a domesticated animal- but for you only (it remains undomesticated in its response to other creatures). Additionally, you may use this ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," as a mount, as per the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ride"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ride","referenceId":"reference:439efdc566bb419f"}," skill, provided that it is at least one size category larger than you and has a comfortable place for you to sit.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Detonating Blast"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["This section was titled Detonate in its official source, but has been renamed to distinguish it from the similarly named \"",{"tag":"a","children":["Detonate"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Detonate","referenceId":"reference:63b9de4f44f858cf"},".\""]}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Blast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Blast","referenceId":"reference:23c844653bfd80fe"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When you use the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Blast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Blast","referenceId":"reference:23c844653bfd80fe"}]}," Force Power, you can spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," to compare the result of your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check to the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of all other characters, creatures, and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," within 2 squares of your target. If you exceed the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of those secondary targets, they also take damage from the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Blast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Blast","referenceId":"reference:23c844653bfd80fe"}]},", and if you fail to exceed their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},", they take half damage instead. This is considered to be an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attack"}," against the secondary targets (but not against the original target).\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Hive Mind"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You can use the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Telepathy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Telepathy"}," application of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," skill as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", and you automatically succeed (no roll required) if your target is a willing recipient on the same planet.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Infuse Weapon"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You can spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," to infuse an unpowered melee weapon (one that does not require an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Energy Cell"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Energy_Cell","referenceId":"reference:a3dedb9c17e4ee9d"},") with the strength of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", making it resistant to the attacks of other weapons. Infusing the weapon takes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"},". From that point forward, when you wield the weapon, its ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"}," is doubled, and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsabers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsabers","referenceId":"reference:420c60d0a682943a"}," do not ignore the weapon's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},". When you spend a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Force Point"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Point"}," to modify the attack roll of an ",{"tag":"b","children":["Infused Weapon"]},", you also add 2 x the Force Point's result to the damage roll if the attack succeeds.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Sickening Blast"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Prerequisite:"]}," ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Blast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Blast","referenceId":"reference:23c844653bfd80fe"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When you use the ",{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Blast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Blast","referenceId":"reference:23c844653bfd80fe"}]}," Force Power, if your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use the Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_the_Force","referenceId":"reference:74883d1dd46b87fe"}," check exceeds the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},", you can choose to move the target -1 step along the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"},". Doing so increases your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Score"}," by 1.\n"]},"\n"]}}
